  <section id="summary">
    <h2>Summary</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        Born in 1900 in the village of Mansure in the Golan, Syria, to a
        Circassian family.
      </li>
      <li>
        Primary school in Quneitra, secondary school in Damascus and Beirut,
        then further study in France.
      </li>
      <li>
        In France he worked on matters concerning Caucasian émigrés in Paris,
        Berlin, Prague and Warsaw, and held a post in the Caucasus Mountaineers’
        People’s Party.
      </li>
      <li>
        Back in Syria, he stood as a candidate for mayor of Quneitra.
      </li>
      <li>
        He played a large part in opening a Circassian school, and worked to
        open branches in Reyhaniye, Hışniye and Adnaniye.
      </li>
      <li>
        He wrote for the newspaper <em>Marg</em>, which appeared in Circassian,
        French, Arabic and Turkish.
      </li>
      <li>He died in 1952.</li>
      <li>
        Works listed (titles only): Circassian Alphabet; Circassian Poems;
        History of the Circassians from the Past to the Present; The
        Circassians in Their Wars against the Tsars; Introduction to Circassian
        History.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>
